+- **Personal Markdown editor**: with `mods/rich-document` installed, Cmd-click
+  (Ctrl-click off macOS) on a local terminal's existing `.md`, `.markdown`,
+  `.mdown` or `.mkd` file opens a document mod tab in that pane's space.
+  Local `file://` URLs work too. Other links and remote-terminal links keep
+  the system opener. This is a personal build customization.
+  The personal macOS host also provides `WebViewState.new({asset_root, entry?})`
+  and `WebView.new(state)` for bundled document editors. Assets stay inside
+  the canonical, read-granted asset root; page network access and navigation
+  are blocked. Subscribe with `state.on("message", (text, cx) => ...)`, then
+  send strings with `state.post_message(text)` after the page reports ready.
+  The page uses `window.ipc.postMessage(text)` and window `message` events.
+  This retained page keeps its scroll, DOM selection and undo across tabs.
